{
  "id": "kirchhoff_s_voltage_and_current_laws",
  "title": "Kirchhoff's Voltage and Current Laws",
  "description": "A tool for analyzing electric circuits using Kirchhoff's Current Law (KCL) and Kirchhoff's Voltage Law (KVL). Calculate unknown currents and voltages in circuit junctions and loops.",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Kirchhoff's Laws Calculator\n\n### Kirchhoff's Current Law (KCL)\nAt any junction in an electric circuit, the total current flowing towards the junction is equal to the total current flowing away from the junction.\n\n**Formula:** Σ I = I₁ + I₂ + ... + Iₙ = 0\n\n### Kirchhoff's Voltage Law (KVL)\nIn a closed loop in a network, the sum of the voltage drops around the loop is zero.\n\n**Formula:** Σ U = U₁ + U₂ + ... + Uₙ = 0"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "headers": [
        "Kirchhoff's Current Law Analysis"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "i1",
          "label": "Current I₁",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.1,
          "unit": "A"
        },
        {
          "id": "i2",
          "label": "Current I₂",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.2,
          "unit": "A"
        },
        {
          "id": "i3",
          "label": "Current I₃",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.1,
          "unit": "A"
        },
        {
          "id": "i4",
          "label": "Current I₄",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": -0.05,
          "unit": "A"
        },
        {
          "id": "i5",
          "label": "Current I₅",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": -0.15,
          "unit": "A"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "i_total",
          "label": "Total Current (Sum of Known Currents)",
          "formula": "inputs.i1 + inputs.i2 + inputs.i3 + inputs.i4 + inputs.i5",
          "unit": "A",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "i6",
          "label": "Unknown Current I₆ (from KCL)",
          "formula": "-(inputs.i1 + inputs.i2 + inputs.i3 + inputs.i4 + inputs.i5)",
          "unit": "A",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Current",
        "Value (A)",
        "Direction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "I₁",
          "0.1",
          "Towards junction"
        ],
        [
          "I₂",
          "0.2",
          "Towards junction"
        ],
        [
          "I₃",
          "0.1",
          "Towards junction"
        ],
        [
          "I₄",
          "-0.05",
          "Away from junction"
        ],
        [
          "I₅",
          "-0.15",
          "Away from junction"
        ],
        [
          "I₆",
          "-0.2",
          "Away from junction"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "headers": [
        "Kirchhoff's Voltage Law Analysis"
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "u1",
          "label": "Voltage U₁",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "V"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2",
          "label": "Voltage U₂",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": -5,
          "unit": "V"
        },
        {
          "id": "u3",
          "label": "Voltage U₃",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": -3,
          "unit": "V"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "u_total",
          "label": "Sum of Voltages (KVL Check)",
          "formula": "inputs.u1 + inputs.u2 + inputs.u3",
          "unit": "V",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}